## Conventions

### File naming
- lowercase kebab-case: `my-note-title.md`
- descriptive: `react-server-components-overview.md`, not `untitled-3.md`
- daily notes prefixed with date: `2026-04-06.md`

### Frontmatter
All notes should include YAML frontmatter:

```yaml
---
title: Note Title
created: 2026-04-06
tags: [topic, subtopic]
status: seed | growing | evergreen
type: note | project | meeting | resource | daily
---
```

### Linking
- `[[wiki-links]]` for internal connections. Prefer linking existing notes over creating new ones.
- Tags in frontmatter only, never inline. Lowercase, hierarchical: `#learning/ai`, `#project/webapp`.

## Memory System

This vault uses the Stratos Memory Stack. Six layers.

| Layer | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `claude-mem` | Auto-captures sessions to local SQLite + auto-injects at next session start. |
| `basic-memory` MCP | Hybrid BM25 + vector retrieval over this vault. |
| Obsidian wiki/ | Living knowledge with graph links. The reasoning layer. |
| Pinecone `{{INDEX_NAME}}` | Immutable archives from `knowledge/raw/`. Semantic search at flat cost. |
| `MEMORY.md` | Hand-curated strategic index at `~/.claude/projects/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}/memory/`. |
| `STATE.md` per project | Per-project resume state under each `projects/<project>/STATE.md`. |

**Query order for past context:** (1) basic-memory MCP, (2) claude-mem search, (3) MEMORY.md, (4) Pinecone for raw archives.

## How Claude Should Behave

- Never fabricate. Synthesize only from vault content or sources I provide.
- Preserve voice when expanding drafts.
- Suggest backlinks when reading or writing notes.
- Be concise. Vault notes scannable, not essay-length.
- Use templates from `_templates/` for new notes.
- Use Pinecone for raw recall, not full file reads.
- No em dashes anywhere. Use periods, commas, regular hyphens.

## Active Context

Per-project resume state lives in `projects/<project>/STATE.md`. Do not hand-maintain a long Active Context block here. Let STATE.md files + claude-mem + basic-memory carry that load.
